% Predicates of arity zero hold or do not hold.  One that holds answers a
% row of no values, written as an empty line, and one that does not answers
% no rows; a query with a row stands between them, since the empty row is
% otherwise the empty line that separates one answer from the next.
initialized.
phase(running).
started :- initialized.

started?
phase(P)?
stopped :- initialized, 1 > 2.
stopped?
